invariant: INV-62
file: src/srv_mldsa.c
catches: test/e2e.sh
builds: bin/tlsclient_tcp_nonblocking bin/tlsclient bin/tlsclient_ecdsa bin/tlsclient_ca bin/tlsclient_ca_ecdsa bin/tlsclient_webpki bin/tlsclient_webpki_aes bin/tlsclient_webpki_aes_extern bin/tlsclient_pq bin/tlsclient_cnsa2 bin/tlsclient_cnsa2_tcp_nonblocking bin/tlsclient_cnsa2_mldsa bin/tlsclient_cnsa2_ca_mldsa bin/example_psk bin/example_pinned bin/example_ca bin/example_webpki bin/pemkey bin/pemkey_ecdsa bin/tlsserver bin/tlsserver_aes bin/tlsserver_aes_extern bin/tlsserver_cnsa2
reason: the server's ML-DSA-87 CertificateVerify content takes 48 bytes of
  transcript hash under a SHA-256 suite, 16 bytes past the hash, so every
  client refuses the signature. No in-process test signs a whole
  CertificateVerify over a live transcript, so the e2e lanes against
  bin/tlsserver_aes hold it: OpenSSL's s_client verifies the signature
  under TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 and TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256.

--- old
    } else {
        wb_bytes(&w, transcript_hash, SHA256_LEN);
    }
--- new
    } else {
        wb_bytes(&w, transcript_hash, SHA384_LEN);
    }
